--- body ---
## Context

Author-ratified design (2026-06-05), companion to the recognition matrix
(0373): an annex table placed AFTER the matrix figure, explaining why
the recall task is hard. The reference list composition by status
(vietnam_thermal_v1.csv, n=163): proposed 62, operational 57,
planned 21, cancelled 11, constructing 10, retired 2. 38% of the list
is *proposed* plants — exactly what memory-based recall won't know.

## Spec (ratified)

One row per status, columns:
- status
- n plants in the reference list (and share of list)
- mean recognition rate across runs — over all (run x plant) cells
  where the plant has this status: fraction recognized (TP). Same run
  set as the matrix: Exp 1 direct/p1-base, all models x all 5 reps.

Counts come from the reference at build time (no hardcoded 163 / 62 —
the v2 adoption (0413) will change them and the DAG rebuild must pick
them up).

## Data path (author directive 2026-06-05)

Build from this table's **own view of the data mart** — the same
upstream source 0373 reads, queried independently. Figure and table
agree by **common cause** (shared mart), not by producer-consumer
chaining: NO side-output consumption, no coupling to 0373's artifacts.
Derive the per-(run x plant) recognition from the mart/records layer
and join with the reference status column. If a shared derivation
helper is warranted, it lives in `src/aedist/` as library code both
scripts import — never as an intermediate file one script writes for
the other.

## Implementation

- `src/aedist/tabulate_status_difficulty.py` — argparse
  (--measurements/--records inputs, --reference, --output), reference
  path from config (0419 ratchet applies).
- Wire in render.mk as a committed handoff artifact
  `report/inputs/generated/tab_status_difficulty.tex`; include in the
  report annex right after the matrix figure.

## First test

```python
def test_status_difficulty_rates():
    # synthetic: 2 statuses, 2 plants each, 2 runs
    # plant A (operational) hit in 2/2 runs, B (operational) 1/2,
    # C, D (proposed) 0/2 -> operational 0.75, proposed 0.0
    rows = build_status_table(matrix_fixture, reference_fixture)
    assert rows["operational"] == (2, 0.75)
    assert rows["proposed"] == (2, 0.0)
```

## Exit criteria

- [x] Table generated from its own mart view + reference, no
      hardcoded counts, no consumption of 0373 artifacts
- [x] Committed handoff artifact + report annex inclusion after the
      matrix figure
- [x] Unit test above green; `make check` passes

